      "writtenOn": "2026-04-08T02:12:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`reg` is a Devicetree conversion for indexing. They are commonly used in Zephyr, e.g. `named-usbc-port` [1]:\n```\n        usbc {  \n                #address-cells \u003d \u003c1\u003e;\n                #size-cells \u003d \u003c0\u003e;\n\n                /* Reg property is used to assign a port number */\n                port0@0 {\n                        compatible \u003d \"named-usbc-port\";\n                        reg \u003d \u003c0\u003e;\n                        bc12 \u003d \u003c\u0026bc12_port0\u003e;\n                };\n                port1@1 {\n                        compatible \u003d \"named-usbc-port\";\n                        reg \u003d \u003c1\u003e;\n                        bc12 \u003d \u003c\u0026bc12_port1\u003e;\n                };\n        };\n```\n\nThis matches the `named-usbc-port` definition better.\n\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/dts/bindings/usbc/named-usbc-port.yaml",
      "parentUuid": "5c3ebfc2_06674cf8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 19,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 19,
        "endChar": 7
      },
